{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q680191","formula":"CCl₄S","hill":"CCl4S","elements":["C","S","Cl"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"S":1.0,"Cl":4.0},"names":{"en":"Perchloromethylmercaptan","ru":"Трихлорметансульфенилхлорид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Trichloromethane sulfenyl chloride or perchloromethyl mercaptan is the organosulfur compound with the formula Cl3C−S−Cl. It is mainly used as an intermediate for the synthesis of dyes and fungicides (captan, folpet). It is a colorless oil, although commercial samples are yellowish.","ru":"Трихлорметансульфенилхлорид — сераорганическое соединение с химической формулой Cl3C-S-Cl. В основном используется в качестве промежуточного продукта при синтезе красителей и фунгицидов (каптан, фолпет). Представляет собой бесцветную маслянистую жидкость, однако коммерческие образцы имеют желтоватый оттенок."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":11666,"mass":185.9,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(SCl)(Cl)(Cl)Cl","inchikey":"RYFZYYUIAZYQLC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"trichloromethyl thiohypochlorite","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11666","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.431,"y":1.065,"z":1.433,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.478,"y":0.99,"z":-1.488,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.023,"y":-0.92,"z":0.048,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-2.51,"y":0.057,"z":-0.001,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.902,"y":-1.191,"z":0.008,"el":"S"},{"x":0.48,"y":-0.001,"z":0.0,"el":"C"}],"bonds":[[0,5,1],[1,5,1],[2,5,1],[3,4,1],[4,5,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q680191","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trichloromethane_sulfenyl_chloride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B